{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Or three witnesses.</b> Since it is written regarding judgment: 'after the majority to incline,' Scripture explains to you regarding witnesses that one does not follow the majority with them, but rather their testimony is nullified — and likewise even if they are a hundred — specifically when they all came to testify and their intention from the outset was to testify. But if two came to testify and warned concerning the matter, and a relative or disqualified witness saw with them — this does not nullify the testimony of the two on account of the seeing of this one, since his intention was not to testify. For if you do not say thus, you will never find two valid witnesses for kiddushin, for behold, how many relatives see at kiddushin? And many times I saw my master the Rav, who would say at the time of kiddushin: 'All who are fit to testify shall be witnesses to the kiddushin.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:04.027880906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}